"recovery plan","recovery plan"]]}]},{"tag":"Leitura","title":"Reading · An academic summary","blocks":[{"type":"text","title":"Summary: Tourism After the Storm","paras":["In 2022 a storm **broke** several bridges. Tourism **was** low, but locals **became** active: they **began** repairs, **brought** food to workers and **bought** local goods.","Researchers **hoped** to learn how towns recover. Their report **was** positive: visitors **were** back within a year."],"kicker":"ACADEMIC SUMMARY","by":"Coastal Research Group","gloss":[["repair","reparo"],["recover","recuperar-se"],["goods","produtos"],["locals","moradores"]]}]},{"tag":"Compreensão","title":"Did you understand?","blocks":[{"type":"tfng","title":"","items":[{"q":"The storm broke bridges.","ans":"T","why":"“broke several bridges.”"},{"q":"Tourism was high after the storm.","ans":"F","why":"“was low.”"},{"q":"Visitors returned within a year.","ans":"T","why":"“within a year.”"}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Vocabulary in context","items":[{"q":"“recover” means…","opts":["recuperar-se","destruir","pagar"],"ans":0,"why":"recover."},{"q":"“goods” means…","opts":["produtos","bondes","jogos"],"ans":0,"why":"goods."}]}]},{"tag":"Gramática","title":"Irregular verbs 1","blocks":[{"type":"table","head":["Base","Passado","Particípio"],"rows":[["be","**was / were**","**been**"],["become","**became**","**become**"],["begin","**began**","**begun**"],["break","**broke**","**broken**"],["bring","**brought**","**brought**"],["buy","**bought**","**bought**"]],"cap":"Irregular verbs 1"},{"type":"box","kind":"look","t":"Regra","body":"Particípio é usado no Present Perfect (B1); por ora, domine o passado."}]},{"tag":"Prática","title":"Practice","blocks":[{"type":"gap","title":"Complete the sentences","bank":null,"items":[{"s":"The storm ___ the bridge. (break)","a":"broke","why":"break-broke."},{"s":"Locals ___ active. (become)","a":"became","why":"become-became."},{"s":"They ___ repairs. (begin)","a":"began","why":"begin-began."},{